# Perl review

When **reviewing or editing** Perl (`*.pm`, `*.t`, `*.pl`, etc.), follow **`perl-style.mdc`** for layout, refs, DBI `0E0`, and the full style guide.

## Do not flag undef dereference chains as crashes

Since Perl 5.10, array-index and hash-key dereference on **undef** yields `undef`, not a fatal error. Chained `->{'key'}` / `->[$i]` through a missing link is normal control flow.

Do not suggest guards, intermediate variables, or "unsafe dereference" findings solely because a chain like `->{'rows'}->[0]->{'id'}` might hit undef. Do not report hash-key or array-index chains as crashes, runtime errors, or “unsafe dereference” findings. Do not recommend hardening unless the change genuinely improves readability — not for safety.

Treat `//`, `defined`, and explicit `throw` as the intended handling downstream — not a bug to fix in the chain itself.

```markdown
# BAD review comment — never write this
Medium — unsafe domain_list access: ->[0] on empty rows will throw before // 'Unavailable'
```

Repo-local copies under `<repo>/.cursor/rules/**/perl-review.mdc` are deprecated; install rules from this repository into `~/.cursor/rules/` instead.
